---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---
<BaseLayout
  title="SkanPay - QR Checkout Gateway"
  description="SkanPay helps merchants and payment partners coordinate QR checkout requests, customer approval, coupon or voucher logic, and merchant-readable results."
  activePath="/"
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div>
      <div class="hero-brand-line">
        <img src="/skanpay-logo.svg" alt="" aria-hidden="true" />
        <span>QR payment gateway</span>
      </div>
      <h1>QR checkout that shows what happened</h1>
      <p class="hero-copy">
        SkanPay turns a scan into a visible checkout flow: request created, customer reviewed, partner logic handled, and store result returned.
      </p>
      <div class="button-row">
        <a class="button primary" href="/contact/">Contact SkanPay</a>
        <a class="button secondary" href="/beamcash-demo/">View BeamCash</a>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-check-list" aria-label="SkanPay checkout priorities">
        <span>Staff can read the status</span>
        <span>Customers see what they approve</span>
        <span>Partners know their handoff</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <aside class="checkout-console" aria-label="SkanPay checkout state example">
      <div class="console-header">
        <div>
          <span>Checkout session</span>
          <strong>QR-2847</strong>
        </div>
        <p>Store-facing state</p>
      </div>
      <div class="console-flow">
        <article>
          <span>Request</span>
          <strong>Amount, merchant, and session reference created</strong>
          <p>Open</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span>Scan</span>
          <strong>Customer opens the payment request</strong>
          <p>Pending</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span>Handoff</span>
          <strong>Wallet, payment, or redemption logic responds</strong>
          <p>Ready</p>
        </article>
      </div>
      <div class="console-result">
        <span>Result</span>
        <strong>Confirmed / redeemed / cancelled / expired</strong>
      </div>
    </aside>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Pain points</p>
        <h2>A scan is not enough. The store needs a result.</h2>
      </div>
      <p>
        SkanPay focuses on the state and handoff around QR checkout so the store, customer, and partner systems can agree on what happened.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="pain-grid compact-grid">
      <article class="pain-card">
        <span>At the counter</span>
        <h3>"Did it go through?"</h3>
        <p>SkanPay gives staff a readable checkout state instead of leaving the scan as a guess.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="pain-card">
        <span>On the phone</span>
        <h3>"What am I approving?"</h3>
        <p>The customer sees merchant and checkout context before approving the request.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="pain-card">
        <span>With offers</span>
        <h3>"Did the value apply?"</h3>
        <p>Coupon or voucher logic can be coordinated inside the checkout handoff.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="pain-card">
        <span>For partners</span>
        <h3>"Where do we fit?"</h3>
        <p>Wallet, payment, loyalty, and merchant systems get clearer responsibility boundaries.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section technical-band">
    <div class="process-layout">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">How it works</p>
        <h2>Four states make the flow easy to review</h2>
        <p class="section-intro">
          The model is simple in a meeting and specific enough for integration planning.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="homepage-flow-grid" aria-label="SkanPay checkout flow">
        <article>
          <span>01</span>
          <h3>Create request</h3>
          <p>The merchant starts a QR checkout request with amount, reference, and session details.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span>02</span>
          <h3>Customer scans</h3>
          <p>The customer opens a checkout prompt and reviews the request before approving.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span>03</span>
          <h3>Coordinate logic</h3>
          <p>Payment, wallet, coupon, or voucher rules are evaluated in the handoff.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span>04</span>
          <h3>Return result</h3>
          <p>The merchant receives a state such as confirmed, redeemed, cancelled, or expired.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section demo-preview">
    <div class="demo-preview-copy">
      <div class="beamcash-logo-plate">
        <img class="beamcash-wordmark" src="/beamcash/beamcash-logo.svg" alt="BeamCash" />
      </div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Demo app under SkanPay</p>
      <h2>BeamCash shows the checkout flow in product form</h2>
      <p class="section-intro">
        BeamCash is the SkanPay demo app for seller setup, QR display, and buyer approval.
      </p>
      <div class="mini-flow-list" aria-label="BeamCash demo flow">
        <span>Set up seller</span>
        <span>Display QR</span>
        <span>Review checkout</span>
      </div>
      <a class="button primary" href="/beamcash-demo/">View Demo</a>
    </div>
    <div class="demo-screens" aria-label="BeamCash demo screens">
      <figure>
        <img src="/beamcash/beamcash-seller-dashboard-mobile.png" alt="BeamCash seller dashboard with QR code" />
        <figcaption>Seller QR dashboard</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure>
        <img src="/beamcash/beamcash-buyer-checkout-mobile.png" alt="BeamCash buyer checkout screen" />
        <figcaption>Buyer checkout</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section homepage-faq">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Questions</p>
        <h2>Short answers before a deeper conversation</h2>
      </div>
      <p>
        Kept brief so the site stays easy to scan.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-list">
      <details>
        <summary>What does SkanPay do?</summary>
        <p>SkanPay is focused on QR checkout coordination: request creation, customer approval, optional redemption logic, and merchant-readable results.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Is SkanPay replacing existing processors?</summary>
        <p>SkanPay is presented as a gateway and coordination layer. Processor or acquirer details depend on the integration model.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Why show BeamCash?</summary>
        <p>BeamCash gives partners a concrete demo of seller setup, QR display, and customer checkout approval.</p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cta-band">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Next step</p>
      <h2>Bring QR payment conversations into focus.</h2>
      <p>Share the merchant, partner, or product details you want SkanPay to support and the team can follow up directly.</p>
    </div>
    <a class="button secondary" href="/contact/">Start a Conversation</a>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
